# ---- Local databases / caches ----
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
!evals/fixtures/*.db
.cache/
tmp/
.tmp/

# ---- Pipeline artifacts (regenerable, sometimes large) ----
data/cache/
data/raw/
evals/reports/*.json
!evals/reports/.gitkeep
# latest.json is the artefact the evaluation dashboard renders, so it is committed
# on purpose. Ad-hoc reports written to any other name stay ignored.
!evals/reports/latest.json
# Screenshots ARE committed. They were ignored while they were 2x captures at ~2MB
# each; the capture script now defaults to 1x, which is sharp at the width a README
# renders them and small enough that six of them do not dominate the repository.
# manifest.json records which provider produced the data behind each capture, so a
# committed image cannot quietly misrepresent fixture data as real weather.

# ---- MLflow (local only; the tracking store is never committed) ----
# The default local backend store and the artifact directory MLflow creates beside
# it. Both are machine-local telemetry, they can hold prompt and response text, and
# nothing in the application reads them.
mlflow.db
mlflow.db-journal
mlruns/
mlartifacts/

# ---- Editors / OS ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~
